{"title":"2017 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (cheese)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8056479593935efd2a6478b077a748ce8ad40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3, BC=2, CD=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"203\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73e9c9486954873b6a269cd3c4aaa53c97f4f91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=8$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb342c5e58a66e0e506e16d591c961a76944370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DX}{BD} = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/72480147975c8e4f661735140db11d8b6e6f485b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BY}{BD} = \\frac{11}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> and the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that lies on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e579e484ef043e8e5adb6cfff36b0e42487e19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF\\cdot XG$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6983ea990c8e8151fdc0e0e9417fe992890d3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }17\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{59 - 5\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{91 - 12\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{67 - 10\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"595\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d6faf33a7ae8609902322f2ef4ae05f7ca9526a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(8cm); real r = 4.01754; draw(circle((0,0), r)); pair C = r * dir(-30), B = r * dir(28.83-30), A = r * dir(72.68-30), D = r * dir(241.98-30); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(B--D); pair X = B * 1/4 + D * 3/4, Y = B * 25/36 + D * 11/36; label(&quot;A&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;B&quot;, B, NE); label (&quot;C&quot;, C, E); label(&quot;D&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;Y&quot;, Y, N); label(&quot;X&quot;, X, N); pair G = X * 1.445 - C*0.445; label(&quot;G&quot;, G, NW); pair E = Y + (D - A) * 1.48; draw(Y--E); draw(A--E); label(&quot;E&quot;, E, S); pair F = E + (A - C)  * 1.45; draw(C--F--E); label(&quot;F&quot;,F,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"378\" height=\"348\" />\n~raxu, put in by fuzimiao2013\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the given ratios, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410f417f9d9688008d872841cfb3469ad9b7885d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XY}{BD} = 1 - \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{11}{36} = \\frac{4}{9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By AA Similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790933e50c3df2d83cd1289861b00fb078d92ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AXD \\sim \\triangle EXY$\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" /> with a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9aa2b3fb5f152edf3e4f39f827911e1c763158c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DX}{XY} = \\frac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe62973349e7d700817905b0aa3d4ff68d12c848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX \\sim \\triangle EFX$\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" /> with a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95d9fb9b0fff1675642ce08b32283d58a838318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AX}{XE} = \\frac{DX}{XY} = \\frac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9df2c8009faca3288d3ffc5cafda386d92267e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XF}{CX} = \\frac{16}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Now we find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Because the quadrilateral is cyclic, we can simply use the Law of Cosines. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/29542c351a72781439e8e161820a35b031f8615b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD^2=3^2+8^2-48\\cos\\angle BAD=2^2+6^2-24\\cos (180-\\angle BAD)=2^2+6^2+24\\cos\\angle BAD\\]\" width=\"661\" height=\"19\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34cf2d3001695d3062ac78f2394da65b086811f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\rightarrow \\cos\\angle BAD = \\frac{11}{24}\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"37\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4808bd72cb90bda57cb7d70cfb0314568b0874a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\rightarrow BD=\\sqrt{51}\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />\nBy Power of a Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558d647c33323a5ed43a0538142c432b7351aefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX\\cdot XG = DX\\cdot XB = \\frac{\\sqrt{51}}{4} \\frac{3\\sqrt{51}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"281\" height=\"41\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/224767b8c0318c94d2b9f80b9176ecfdc5a5b9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF\\cdot XG = \\frac{XF}{CX} CX\\cdot XG = \\frac{51}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 17}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"347\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>-solution by FRaelya\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We shall make use of the pairs of similar triangles present in the problem, Ptolemy's Theorem, and Power of a Point. \nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. First, from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> being a cyclic quadrilateral, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e085ba8a93ed5f25197654f5b18f1cfc700790a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCZ \\sim \\triangle AZD$\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f606ba420c0b87da8f9549c292a69641046d3fc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BZA \\sim \\triangle CDZ$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6f5a22a58b6a68df67628ba91a9bc3b67dbf80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{BZ} = \\frac{8}{AZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705eb231622ec6d9c8d40ee8f7fa1a2ea2482f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{CZ} = \\frac{3}{BZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe16be2ca71fcd688d532a0b388a45e88bc18a2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{CZ} = \\frac{8}{DZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/5/f85ffda427fb55c41b535c67ad8b429fad371a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BZ = \\frac{1}{2}CZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/4887cc2c1a7989f7fc6b3fa8654baa4c898988c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AZ = 2CZ$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21bb4370f96512ab9aed940cf56eb394dda146a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DZ = 4CZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />. By Ptolemy's Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac19df806076cff70169140e4f7a4ae29fbd762.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(AB)(CD) + (BC)(DA) = (AC)(BD) = (AZ + ZC)(BZ + ZD)\\]\" width=\"488\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6ac3080949ef44eba9b1c1272c073a84886ba6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\rightarrow 3 \\cdot 6 + 2 \\cdot 8 = 34 = \\left(2CZ + ZC\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}CZ + 4CZ\\right) = \\frac{27}{2}CZ^2.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"43\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a502dc2423db389d29891c9cb03ee7766a1144c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CZ^2 = \\frac{68}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" />. Then, by Power of a Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb0f522c992181e902584fc36ddfe4041b80294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GX \\cdot XC = BX \\cdot XD = \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}BD^2 = \\frac{3}{16} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{9}{2}CZ\\right)^2 = \\frac{9 \\cdot 17}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"477\" height=\"46\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b718e0b1264057ba08e209f63b1e7edf95aac45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XG = \\frac{9 \\cdot 17}{16XC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />.\nNext, observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe62973349e7d700817905b0aa3d4ff68d12c848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX \\sim \\triangle EFX$\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a573185a6614f1e962c860fb7dc023967a526a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XE}{XF} = \\frac{AX}{XC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"39\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38a23a7e24ce36c468da2d44d2ca3d526524645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AXD} \\sim \\triangle{EXY}$\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f18eb609724e0a8da516548394719e48c948238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{AX} = \\frac{EY}{XE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" />. We can compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdabdb3e888bb42480ff436d2e6f86bfc5d683d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EY = \\frac{128}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" /> after noticing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e712bd449396ea63dc918c5b8ab3e825c46a13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = BD - BY - DX = BD - \\frac{11}{36}BD - \\frac{1}{4}BD = \\frac{4}{9}BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"453\" height=\"37\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc18816353eef90bb21de6a73901964558a0d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{DX} = \\frac{32}{BD} = \\frac{EY}{XY} = \\frac{EY}{\\frac{4}{9}BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"221\" height=\"44\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d988cb104b3f4651f82fdae07622c719601e98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{AX} = \\frac{128}{9XE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0baa5b36ca137763c808173b090ace1303c193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XE}{AX} = \\frac{XF}{XC} = \\frac{16}{9} \\rightarrow XF = \\frac{16}{9}XC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"276\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Multiplying our equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/684ddc7ebf8968e63d288df2b06a1871d585a764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8404db180a248e3e2cbbdde9c3b5cf31a2bb27e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97c41da87e2ed41d171f4a1a03fc90e96b45c64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF \\cdot XG = \\frac{9 \\cdot 17}{16XC} \\cdot \\frac{16}{9}XC = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 17}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"310\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to be the intersection between line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86af7245c8f18e57b263f69de508816efb0e6fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GFE = \\angle ACG = \\angle APG = 180 - \\angle GPE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"346\" height=\"16\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/39826b3ad51ef9db1cced122cd7e1e4abd814bae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GFE + \\angle GDE = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"189\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32df34e350748dbabe4634f784161fcecfe4ada0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PEFG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral. Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Power of a Point\">Power of a Point</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e92482ad4521cf57083f5a67c9bea419646936a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XP \\cdot XE = XG \\cdot XF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f92828d2542797f8fb8232e9eba7e41ec6ee8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADX \\sim \\triangle EYX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe62973349e7d700817905b0aa3d4ff68d12c848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX \\sim \\triangle EFX$\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b749fd9d583ec1b2d9d198b62c5be196bf8c03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX/XE = XD/YX = 9/16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />. Using Power of a Point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/29663f75ce67b89f497d1a1ebb75dc356e38eca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AX)(PX) = (BX)(DX)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f08f5a1a75f5d82e0f47c13b424987cf066ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=9/16 XE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24aaad68078f81df5b861c934e92669f4b648905.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{9}{16}(XE)(PX) = (BX)(DX) = \\dfrac{9}{16}(FX)(GX)\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"37\" />\nBy <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a60037044f84e6124fc396f103ba530d3cef70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = \\sqrt{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />, as in Solution 1. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d71ab0f1682cd0780242b2d298ee299c06f3003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = 3/4 (\\sqrt{51})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/54143816b1a67cac190a91ed34be6ef616a2ef06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DX = 1/4 (\\sqrt{51})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"24\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/f/94f5a2e8f69a53222b73ef9162947293577475ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9}{16}(FX)(GX) = \\left( \\dfrac{\\sqrt{51}}{4}\\right)\\left( \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{51}}{4}\\right) = \\dfrac{3(51)}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"351\" height=\"55\" />. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08bcd4f0df23beeb8bae70a79c1f79c94ab91715.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FX \\cdot GX = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"165\" height=\"30\" /> as a result.\n</p><p>-Solution by sml1809\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>You could have also got the relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e92482ad4521cf57083f5a67c9bea419646936a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XP \\cdot XE = XG \\cdot XF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" /> as follows: From the similarities, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8de9d9ba80f5b65a0c6b9576b747f97087815a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX/XE = CX/XF = 9/16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"20\" />. PoP on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417916e99c253a59209313339f29e832b7e173e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AX)(PX) = (CX)(GX)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39128c3dc4452233985aa6c4d6c18b5a9063b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = 9/16 XE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a40e4742945bd2f6e5798be0d4da26c84ded77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX=9/16 FX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a00f336e1c866594909eb86281f55b72c4b1a7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9/16 (XE)(PX) = 9/16(FX)(GX),\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"18\" />\nimplying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b9e96672b2efe823f1d724f45f560a1ba02fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(XP)(XE) = (XG)(XP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~sml1809\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048310e281a424a8bbf36e23e04010fb1f30963f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c553c571de4c37c7a984d07326978a69169c6f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \t\\parallel EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee85ced543e22b203202898ce83630bd6c935775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad \\therefore$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe62973349e7d700817905b0aa3d4ff68d12c848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX \\sim \\triangle EFX$\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/2937e7283b9c1a73c385a6a6aeeb0a34b1f9b1aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad \\frac{XF}{XC} = \\frac{XE}{XA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>By Power of a Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/55139a24a4142a140cf48e531e3df7d318f91380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XG \\cdot XC = XD \\cdot XB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"177\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>By multiplying the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equations we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee501107c33e3ab60779f30d4d8ca75455874522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF \\cdot XG = \\frac{XE}{XA} \\cdot XD \\cdot XB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048310e281a424a8bbf36e23e04010fb1f30963f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdbef693cd4a8b1ce98bc280405401d37671a32f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YE \t\\parallel AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee85ced543e22b203202898ce83630bd6c935775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad \\therefore$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f3885420929f0ba9b45d29f87235bb34e60680ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EYX \\sim \\triangle ADX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/653708bc4edee4463bfb80791dbdc35884231d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad \\frac{XD}{XY} = \\frac{XA}{XE}, \\quad XD \\cdot XE = XA \\cdot XY, \\quad XD = \\frac{XA \\cdot XY}{XE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"469\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>By substitution, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc66df35cbb769ce69b6ec1c0626a6034d1f45e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XF \\cdot XG = \\frac{XE}{XA} \\cdot \\frac{XA \\cdot XY}{XE} \\cdot XB = XY \\cdot XB = \\frac{4}{9} BD \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} BD = \\frac{BD^2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"561\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f45ff5abb939b05f1f20d2c6326fb7a09dd045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = AB$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b042926d7c8afb355ad301775d381ef235da82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ce4e04a1242d797b57bef0f67f88278185830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bdd2d2eb17088106def067beedb59317ca4d071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2df1fc4909ecffb13b89a45e7c65ee424721b553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb8438ed83af4be97dccfe55d189e4ca004a94d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By Ptolemy's theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5989e0914d742efc76c7833d1879708227f99f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\cdot q = a \\cdot c + b \\cdot d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19a8ed1d6d534154dd24afec22161b415b4139d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABD] = \\frac12 \\cdot ad \\cdot \\sin A, \\quad [BCD] = \\frac12 \\cdot bc \\cdot \\sin C = \\frac12 \\cdot bc \\cdot \\sin A\\]\" width=\"490\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace0be7a936200191f7f49234a4cf7850175c70e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC] = \\frac12 \\cdot ab \\cdot \\sin B, \\quad [ACD] = \\frac12 \\cdot cd \\cdot \\sin D = \\frac12 \\cdot cd \\cdot \\sin B\\]\" width=\"492\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c4f760f1254c60f4e581aa93bbe8c519ef8f5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABCD] = [ABD] + [BCD] = \\frac12 \\cdot ad \\cdot \\sin A + \\frac12 \\cdot bc \\cdot \\sin A = \\frac12 (ad + bc) \\sin A\\]\" width=\"553\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f58aef6546bb65aae0372e4b95845be922c335.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABCD] = [ABC] + [ACD] = \\frac12 \\cdot ab \\cdot \\sin B + \\frac12 \\cdot cd \\cdot \\sin B = \\frac12 (ab + cd) \\sin B\\]\" width=\"553\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b7a4a516bff4e10342630a9fb8007b83caaf30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ab + cd}{ad + bc} = \\frac{ \\sin A }{ \\sin B} = \\frac{ \\frac{q}{2R} }{ \\frac{p}{2R} } = \\frac{q}{p}, \\quad p = \\frac{q(ad + bc)}{ab + cd}\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d5b3fd30371c4d964d68f831d878ce851dbe7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{q(ad + bc)}{ab + cd} \\cdot q = ac + bd\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1cb4909ea4d96cfcf10dd8b897c4140c78c434.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD^2 = q^2 = \\frac{ (ac + bd)(ab + cd) }{ad + bc} = \\frac{(3 \\cdot 6 + 2 \\cdot 8)(3 \\cdot 2 + 6 \\cdot 8)}{3 \\cdot 8 + 2 \\cdot 6} = 51\\]\" width=\"515\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b77fe4dace0f8049adc0d7f4bb151f912b2e02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XF \\cdot XG = \\frac{51}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 17}\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(cheese)\">Solution 5 (cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> as in the previous solutions, with the Law of Cosines. Once we do this, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4eda56e2a31ede9c2c57cc5e5feaccff71ae1dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}=\\sqrt{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />. Now, note that answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is the only answer that seems to be related to this length, so  the best guess is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7748da70a708efddba8e140d172bf503031667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) 17}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JdERP0d0W64&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvLZmuDnM-0vrFniLpo7Orbp&amp;index=4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JdERP0d0W64&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvLZmuDnM-0vrFniLpo7Orbp&amp;index=4</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A\">2017 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"externa